# Act I Survival & Encounter Gates

Full mechanics: `@system_mechanics.md` §10 (needs), §11 (frame restraint).

## Siphon ≠ food

Leech feels good; it is **not** calories. Hunger and thirst stay real in Unforged. Aeric can feel fed by the rush and still starve.

## Chapter-band gates (locked)

| Band | Focus |
|------|--------|
| **Ch4–5** | **Water** — find, risk dirty source; Mariusz taint/boil **theory** (no Survival Skill UI) |
| **Ch5–7** | **Food** — forage fail → Mariusz edibility lecture → first **cooked** warp-beast meat (gross, necessary) |
| **Ch6–8** | **Crude craft** — bone knife, hide wrap, fire; **cores = fuel/craft after Foundation Siphon**, **never food** |
| **Ch7–10** | Needs ease slightly; full mortal independence **not** gone until **Copper Core** |

## Monster corpses

* Aeric has **no butchery skill** — Mariusz offers **scholar insight** (avoid glands, burn meat, warp-taint).
* No `[Butchery Lvl 1]` unless earned later through repetition + Auditor.
* Eating raw ichor/glands = parasite / sickness risk (Vitality buys slack, not immunity).

## Human contact schedule

| Band | On-page |
|------|---------|
| **Ch4–6** | Echoes only — screams cut short, corpses, scavengers on remains; **no rescue**; Jonah guilt rhymes |
| **Ch7–9** | Distant survivors (silhouettes, overheard fights); optional **one** brief contact — may go wrong |
| **Ch10** | Smoke, trails, fire — humans forming patterns; Act II door |
| **Ch11+** | Act II — templates vs unsealed, real conflict |
| **Not until gated** | Cohen reunion, Wade on-page, Idealistic Rival |

## Chapter 4 outline (author default)

1. Wrong forest / wreckage splinters + **water beat**
2. Mariusz **full sediment flush** (step-by-step)
3. Fight — new mob, **BJJ** body memory, residue-only siphon (Option A — core suppressed)
4. **Meridian 5** attempt (Mariusz guided; success default)
5. Human echo (corpse/scream) — no meeting
6. STATUS with yellow diffs vs Ch3 end

## Mortal needs fade by Realm (summary)

Unforged = hungry/thirsty → Copper reduced → Iron+ food optional (habit) → Silver+ breath/food as anchor. See §10.

## Frame restraint (summary)

Book 1: normal walking (~frame avg ≤20). "Hard to walk normal" ~**25+** / **Iron Core** without Shell Restraint. See §11.
